From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] backports: use kernel QCOM MDT loader

The Qualcomm SoC Makefile in backports already leaves mdt_loader.o
disabled, but QCOM_MDT_LOADER is still declared as a local backports
symbol. ath12k AHB
selecting it therefore targets a deliberately unavailable symbol instead of
the kernel-provided MDT loader.

Drop the unused local definition and local-symbol entry so backports
imports the kernel QCOM_MDT_LOADER value, matching the existing QRTR/MHI
arrangement.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig | 6 ------
 local-symbols            | 1 -
 2 files changed, 7 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig
@@ -69,12 +69,6 @@ config QCOM_KRYO_L2_ACCESSORS
 	bool
 	depends on (ARCH_QCOM || COMPILE_TEST) && ARM64
 
-config QCOM_MDT_LOADER
-	depends on n
-	tristate
-	depends on m
-	depends on QCOM_SCM
-
 config QCOM_OCMEM
 	depends on n
 	tristate "Qualcomm On Chip Memory (OCMEM) driver"
--- a/local-symbols
+++ b/local-symbols
@@ -61,7 +61,6 @@ QCOM_GENI_SE=
 QCOM_GSBI=
 QCOM_LLCC=
 QCOM_KRYO_L2_ACCESSORS=
-QCOM_MDT_LOADER=
 QCOM_OCMEM=
 QCOM_PD_MAPPER=
 QCOM_PDR_HELPERS=
